At equilibrium $\Delta G=0$

\begin{array}{l}

\text { Hence, } \Delta G=\Delta H-T_{e} \Delta S=0 \\

\therefore \Delta H=T_{e} \Delta S \text { or } T_{e}=\frac{\Delta H}{\Delta S}

\end{array}



For a spontaneous reaction $\Delta G$ must be negative which is possible only if $\Delta H-T \Delta S\lt 0\therefore \Delta H\lt T \triangle S$

or $T \gt \frac{\Delta H}{\Delta S} ; T_{e}\lt T$

